  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A catastrophic thermal collapse in the deep waters surrounding The Berg, dated to the latter period of the Great Thaw. The event was triggered when the ancient heat-veins beneath the Corpse Current — an anomalous underwater thermal convergence sacred to the orca Wake-Singers — fractured along their deepest seams, flooding the abyss with superheated water. The orca name for the disaster has become standard usage. No penguin term exists, which tells its own story about whose loss this was.
    
    ## The Collapse
    
    The rupture produced water hot enough to generate steam in the upper channels. Orca shamanic accounts report a sustained sound from the deep lasting three days — described in pressure-song as the voice of their dead god. The acoustic testimony is consistent with large-scale geothermal venting, though the duration is difficult to verify independently.
    
    The collapse killed entire orca pods and boiled the shallow hunting grounds they depended on. The Wake-Singers lost three shamans. In the chaos, the Dreaming Tooth — a sacred artifact carved from their dead god's jaw — passed out of Wake-Singer custody, acquiring new grooves in its surface whose optical properties remain unexplained.
    
    Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute, a senior figure of the Shadow Covens Order who had negotiated the last resource-peace between orca pods and penguin colonies, descended into the thermal vents. Silvsiaelrous~ performed a blood-magic binding to seal the worst fractures and contain M7-6HH39N, a corrupted whale-bone obelisk the deep had begun pushing surfaceward. The ritual required remaining until pressure equalized. Silvsiaelrous~ did not surface. Seventeen penguins died when the lower thermal corridors sheared. The obelisk's containment proved temporary; it required further intervention before its rise was arrested.
    
    ## Consequences on The Berg
    
    The orcas who had maintained deep-water salvage routes to The Berg simply stopped coming. The Aurora Stack and Nightshelf were forced into emergency rationing of fire-cores and aurora-crystals — the first such rationing in a generation.
    
    In the Nightshelf, secondary collapses followed when mining operations at the Glow-Fissure breached into destabilized substrata. Fourteen fire-keepers died in the experimental core chamber at Terrace Momiou. The E'frostlings, a Nightshelf faction, exploited the disarray to reclaim lost territory. The geological events designated Rofundis∴rupt and Profun∴lapsum compounded the destruction, collapsing infrastructure and killing dozens more — including candidates assembled for the selection cycle of the Mask, an artifact requiring a new wielder after Silvsiaelrous~'s death.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771577050779_0", anchor: "passed out of Wake-Singer custody, acquiring new grooves", text: "I wrote in the Dreaming Tooth entry that Grandmother Deep 'simply reminded everyone whose jaw it came from.' The main text here says the Tooth 'passed out of Wake-Singer custody,' as though it were misplaced luggage. Both sentences are mine. One of them is wrong. The ice at the relevant stratum shows the Tooth's pressure-signature *strengthening* during the collapse, not dispersing — consistent with deliberate relocation, not chaotic loss. The passive construction was cowardice. She took it back.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577050779_1", anchor: "descended into the thermal vents", text: "Every orca source I have read — every one — insists no penguin has ever seen the Corpse Current. Its location is shared only among Wake-Singers. Yet here is Silvsiaelrous~, an augur of the Shadow Covens Order, descending into the thermal convergence to perform blood-magic at its seams. Either the orcas' most closely guarded secret was not particularly guarded, or the last resource-peace Silvsiaelrous~ negotiated purchased something the diplomatic record does not mention. How extraordinary that no one finds this remarkable.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577050779_2", anchor: "The orcas who had maintained deep-water salvage routes", text: "One fracture. The heat-veins crack, the orcas stop coming, the rationing begins, the Nightshelf mines destabilize, the fire-keepers die, the E'frostlings advance, the Mask selection collapses. Every subsequent crisis in this entry is a domino falling from the first sentence. I keep trying to find the point where someone intervened rather than merely reacted. It is not here.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
